-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1081, found by an independent re-check: a state reached
-- again at an EARLIER clock is explored again, and what that second visit
-- cannot try must still be said. `k` is reached at clock 2 by 2 events (T lapses
-- at 1, then q at 2) and again at clock 0 by 3 (t, u, q at 0). From clock 2,
-- b's window is [2, 5]: the instants 2, 5 and a gap, 3 in all. From clock 0 it
-- is [0, 5] with a tie at 1 (V's 4 on S1's 5) and a gap, 4 in all, so under
-- `--max-instants 3` it is cut, and only the second visit cuts it.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF T, U, Q, B, V, S1
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF t, u, q, b, v, s1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
k MEANS
       (PARTY B MUST b WITHIN 6 OF 0
          HENCE (PARTY V MUST v WITHIN 4 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY V)
          LEST BREACH BY B)
  RAND (PARTY S1 SHANT s1 WITHIN 5 OF 0 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY S1)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
qk MEANS PARTY Q MUST q WITHIN 1 HENCE k LEST BREACH BY Q

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
rc MEANS
  PARTY T MUST t WITHIN 1
    HENCE (PARTY U MUST u WITHIN 1 HENCE qk LEST BREACH BY U)
    LEST qk

#TRACE rc AT 0 WITH
  PARTY T DOES t AT 0
